<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yusuf IV of Granada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1432">1432</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Ibn al-Mawl</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yusuf IV, known as Ibn al-Mawl, was Nasrid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> for a few months in 1432. Backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-of-castile">John II of Castile</a> after the Castilian victory at La Higueruela, he took power from Muhammad IX and ruled as a Castilian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>, but he soon lost support and was killed when Muhammad IX regained the throne. His brief reign showed how <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> exploited Nasrid divisions.</p></div>
